  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R42 (block 333000): the FOOD LIFECYCLE -- storage, spoilage, preparation, QUANTIZATION. A FoodItem{kind,state(raw/prepared/spoiled),freshness,portions(INTEGER)} in a Larder{cold}, prepared by a COOK (an agent) USING a Kitchen{fuel}, with QUALITY = the cook's skill. fs_spoil: per epoch freshness -= spoil_rate*(cold? cold_factor:1) (kind-specific: fish fast, grain slow, salt-fish slowest; cold preserves). fs_rot: freshness~0 -> spoiled (inedible). fs_prepare: raw + kitchen fuel -> prepared (taste+freshness up, fuel spent); some foods inedible until prepared. fs_eat: consume ONE portion iff edible (not spoiled, prepared if needs_prep); meal value = energy*freshness. fs_reject: spoiled / raw-needing-prep / empty -> refused (no free nutrition from rotten or raw food). Portions are integer -- in-frame quantities are quantized. QUANTIZATION is AGENT-CHOSEN (not fixed units -- the item count is just stock): a Household{members,shares,food} DIVIDES a food quantum among its members -- hq_ration sets per_member = food / shares (the household's chosen split). The household can RE-QUANTIZE (change shares) -- a poor family splits ONE serving of bread among four; a guest arrives and it re-splits finer. Scarcity -> finer quanta (smaller servings). The split is the agent's decision, dynamic and re-quantizable -- the substrate's dynamic quantization, at the table. Spoiled food does NOT disappear -- it persists and is EATABLE (a desperate agent may eat it): fs_eat grades the meal by an EATER -- nutrition = energy*freshness*(raw_penalty if uncooked-needs-prep) (LESS NUTRITIOUS as it spoils), pleasantness = taste*freshness - disgust (MORE UNPLEASANT), illness = accrues with (1-freshness)*rot_illness (+ raw_illness) (CHANCE OF ILLNESS). Only an EMPTY stock yields no food; nothing is hard-rejected -- food is food, just graded from a feast to a sickening scrap. PREPARATION REQUIRES AN AGENT, NOT A KITCHEN (fs_prepare): an agent -preparing-> item -using-> a STATION prepares food ANYWHERE. prep_kind 'season' (add spices) needs NO heat -- done on bare hands / the ground / a bench; prep_kind 'cook' needs a heat source (station.heat>=1: a fire or stove). Quality = cook_skill*(1+station.prep_power) (a better surface helps); cooking spends the station's fuel and lifts freshness + makes needs-prep food edible; both kinds improve taste. A kitchen is NOT required -- only an agent (and heat only IF cooking).",
